10. Collections Framework (Super Useful for DSA)

1. ArrayList :

import java.util.*;
ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add(10);
list.add(20);
System.out.println(list.get(1)); // 20

2 . HashSet :
HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
set.add(1);
set.add(2);
System.out.println(set.contains(1)); // true

3 . HashMap :
HashMap<String, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put("apple", 2);
map.put("banana", 5);
System.out.println(map.get("apple")); // 2

4.Queue :
Queue<Integer> q = new Queue<>();
q.add(10);
q.add(20);
System.out.println(q.poll()); // 10 (Removes)  FIFO - FIRST IN FIRST OUT

5. STACK .
Stack<Integer>  s = new Stack<>();
s.push(10);
s.push(20);
System.out.println(s.pop()); //LIFO Removed 20

// Important Keywords :

static -- belongs to class not object.
final -- constant cannot be changed .
this -- refers to current object .
super -- refers to parent class .

// Time Complexity :
Array Acess  :  O(1)
Array Search : O(n)
HashMap (get/put) : O(1) Average .
Sorting(Array.sort) : O(n log n)

